 linearity means that a system satisfies two essential properties,

15
00:01:14,480 --> 00:01:21,200
 additivity and homogeneity and these are very very well defined. Additivity means that we can build

16
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:26,640
 up responses to complex inputs as the sum of responses to simple inputs. You might have heard

17
00:01:26,640 --> 00:01:31,440
 this said in mathematics as the integral of a sum is the same as the sum of the integrals because

18
00:01:31,440 --> 00:01:37,600
 the integral is a linear operator. This means that if an input is a sum of two things we can

19
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:42,080
 simulate the response to each of those things separately and sum the responses as if we've

20
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:46,880
 simulated for the sum of those inputs to begin with. This means that we can take inputs which are

21
00:01:46,960 --> 00:01:51,440
 nominally complex and might be hard to simulate simulate their parts individually and bring it all

22
00:01:51,440 --> 00:01:56,560
 together at the end. Homogeneity means that we can scale responses and have the same effect as

